{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791626738,"nonce":"688zCjZgD8vieOO28CGrjJjxO4A=","title":"Returning a Null\u003cInt\u003e call result from an Int function returns the box address","message":"`static function f(s:String):Int return Std.parseInt(s);` returns the box pointer.\nIn the Return path (mir stmt/statements.rs), maybe_unbox_optional_for_target treats the\n`*void` register from haxe_std_parse_int_box as a raw payload and bitcasts it; `var`\nunboxes correctly via maybe_unbox_value keyed on the Null\u003cInt\u003e HIR type. Also breaks\n`@:to toInt():Int return Std.parseInt(this)` (Issue3347 shape with an explicit return).\n\nRelated, same round: abstract instance-method calls never apply @:from to their\narguments (`a.add(4)` with `add(k:IntKey)` passes a raw 4 and crashes);\nresolve_callee_formal_param_types (mir resolve.rs) only handles Class receivers.","files":null}]}